WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:08.079
Week 17: Preterite: Completed Events. report what happened sequence completed actions ask follow-up questions

2
00:00:08.079 --> 00:00:14.239
Cultural lens. Oral storytelling, news leads, and how chronology is signaled.

3
00:00:14.239 --> 00:00:26.673
Avoid the single-story trap. Treat country, region, age, relationship, and setting as variables. Describe the evidence you have without turning one example into a universal rule.

4
00:00:26.673 --> 00:00:38.680
Language variation. Recognize regional choices and ask what a form means locally. Use the neutral course model for production until the situation gives you a reason to adapt.

5
00:00:38.680 --> 00:00:47.893
Reflection. Compare this context with one you know. Name one similarity, one difference, and one question that would prevent an assumption.

6
00:00:47.893 --> 00:01:12.700
Model language. Ayer llegué temprano a la oficina. — Yesterday I arrived at the office early. Primero revisamos el informe. — First we reviewed the report. Luego llamaron al supervisor. — Then they called the supervisor. ¿Qué ocurrió después? — What happened afterward? La reunión terminó a las seis. — The meeting ended at six.

7
00:01:12.700 --> 00:01:22.854
Check your readiness. Explain the core idea. Produce an original example. Complete the section assessment at 85% or higher.
